/-!
# Parameter-generic forms of the toy-specific helpers

The toy export (`n = 8`, five primes of `Q_0`, 36 refresh parts, PRF buckets of width two) fixes
several helpers to its parameters: the five-term CRT recombination `part_row`, the width-two
dynamic state read `familyGetDynamic_half` of `PrfCellFlat.rel_1`/`PrfCellFlat.keys_1`, the
eight-coefficient decode loop and output residues, the CRT basis facts of `Dio2Online0Row` proven
by `fin_cases` over every pair, the 36-part index maps and the eight-coefficient readout packing.
This module states each of them for arbitrary parameters, so that the production row
(`n = 2^16`, 27 primes, about `1.7e7` refresh parts, PRF buckets of the PRF layout's width) can
instantiate them without re-proving. The toy lemmas and their callers are unchanged; where cheap,
a `rfl` lemma records that the toy definition is the generic one at the toy parameters.

* `chainSum`, `part_row_gen`: the CRT recombination over a left-nested `matrixAdd` chain of any
  length.
* `familyGetDynamic_div`, `Comp.PrfCellFlat.Comp_1W`, `PrfCellFlat.rel_1W`,
  `PrfCellFlat.keys_1W`: the dynamic PRF cell reading member `⌊i / W⌋` for any bucket width.
* `decode_onehot_loop`, `coeff_val_Xe_gen`, `Xe_mul_Xe_gen`: the decode loop and output residues
  for any ring dimension.
* `crtCertificate`, `crt_hyps_of_certificate`, `crt_hyps_of_pairs`, `prod_eq_listProd`: CRT basis
  hypotheses from one Boolean certificate evaluated by the kernel.
* `readoutMemberN`, `placedReadoutN`, `cellValN` and the smudge/fresh value lemmas for any `n`;
  `partIndexGen`, `smudgePartColumnGen`, `freshPartColumnGen` for any part and prime counts.
-/

